### Description

While the popup is open, `ComboboxPattern` relays navigation and typeahead keys to the popup through a signal: the key handler does `this.keyboardEventRelay.set(e)`, and an effect later re-dispatches the event on the popup's control target. If a second key arrives before the effect runs, the signal is overwritten and the first key is never relayed.

Effects:

- Down, Down, Down pressed quickly moves the active option once.
- Typeahead loses characters: with options `item`, `item-2`, `item-3`, typing `item-3` with no delay between keys lands on `item`; with 60 ms between keys it lands on `item-3`.
- Test automation and tools that send keys in a burst (and some assistive technology input) see wrong results. Seen in Chromium through Playwright, and in unit tests.

Related: #33361 (same relay signal, different symptom: a stale event replayed on reopen).

### Reproduction

```ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { TestBed } from '@angular/core/testing';
import { Combobox, ComboboxPopup, ComboboxWidget } from '@angular/aria/combobox';
import { Listbox, Option } from '@angular/aria/listbox';

@Component({
  imports: [Combobox, ComboboxPopup, ComboboxWidget, Listbox, Option],
  template: `
    <div ngCombobox #combobox="ngCombobox" tabindex="0">Pick one</div>
    <ng-template ngComboboxPopup [combobox]="combobox">
      <div ngListbox ngComboboxWidget #listbox="ngListbox" focusMode="activedescendant"
        [activeDescendant]="listbox.activeDescendant()">
        @for (o of options; track o) {
          <div ngOption [value]="o" [label]="o">{{ o }}</div>
        }
      </div>
    </ng-template>
  `,
})
class Repro {
  options = ['alpha', 'bravo', 'charlie', 'delta'];
}

const key = (el: Element, k: string) =>
  el.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: k, bubbles: true }));

it('handles each key pressed back to back', async () => {
  const fixture = TestBed.createComponent(Repro);
  await fixture.whenStable();
  const combobox = fixture.nativeElement.querySelector('[ngCombobox]');
  combobox.focus();
  key(combobox, 'ArrowDown');            // open
  await fixture.whenStable();
  key(combobox, 'Home');
  await fixture.whenStable();
  key(combobox, 'ArrowDown');
  key(combobox, 'ArrowDown');
  key(combobox, 'ArrowDown');
  await fixture.whenStable();
  const id = combobox.getAttribute('aria-activedescendant');
  expect(fixture.nativeElement.querySelector(`[id="${id}"]`).textContent.trim())
    .toBe('delta');                       // actual: 'bravo'
});
```

### Expected Behavior

Each key event is handled, in order. Three Down presses move three options.

### Actual Behavior

Only the last key since the effect last ran is relayed. Three Down presses move one option ("bravo" in place of "delta").

A possible fix: relay each event synchronously from the key handler (or queue them), not through a single-value signal.

### Environment

- Angular: 22.2.1
- CDK/Material: @angular/cdk 22.2.3, @angular/aria 22.2.3 (also in 22.3.0-next.2 and `main`)
- Browser(s): Chromium (Playwright); Vitest with happy-dom
- Operating System (e.g. Windows, macOS, Ubuntu): macOS
